# Parallax (PLX) Tokenomics

Parallax (PLX) is the native cryptocurrency of the independent Parallax Scrypt Proof-of-Work blockchain.

PLX is created through blockchain mining and can be independently verified using the public Parallax block explorer.

## Live Mined Supply

The current mined PLX supply is determined directly from the live Parallax blockchain.

Official block explorer:

https://explorer.parallaxcoin.xyz/

The live blockchain should be treated as the authoritative source for the amount of PLX currently mined and recorded on-chain.

## Current Block Reward

Current mining reward:

**50 PLX per block**

PLX is distributed through Scrypt Proof-of-Work mining.

There was no separate token contract or ERC-20/BEP-20 issuance because PLX is the native asset of the Parallax blockchain.

## Public Mining

Parallax is designed around public Proof-of-Work mining.

Users running Parallax Core can participate directly in Scrypt mining using the integrated mining interface.

Mining performs two functions:

- Secures the Parallax blockchain
- Distributes newly mined PLX

## Long-Term Economic Model

The original Parallax economic model was designed around a long-term target of:

**1,000,000,000 PLX**

The intended economic allocation model is:

| Allocation | Percentage | Long-Term Target |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| Public Mining | 40% | 400,000,000 PLX |
| Development | 30% | 300,000,000 PLX |
| Liquidity / Exchange Trading | 20% | 200,000,000 PLX |
| Community Rewards | 10% | 100,000,000 PLX |

These figures describe the project's **long-term economic allocation model**.

They should not be interpreted as currently minted or pre-allocated on-chain balances.

## Current On-Chain Supply

The current on-chain PLX supply is created through active blockchain mining.

It can be verified at any time through:

https://explorer.parallaxcoin.xyz/

This means the amount of PLX presently existing on-chain can be checked independently rather than relying on a manually published supply figure.

## Development Allocation

Long-term economic planning reserves up to:

**30% — 300,000,000 PLX**

for project development.

The original model envisages a multi-year development allocation rather than an immediate unrestricted distribution.

Any future implementation or distribution mechanism should be publicly documented before use.

## Liquidity and Exchange Trading

Long-term economic planning reserves up to:

**20% — 200,000,000 PLX**

for exchange liquidity and trading infrastructure.

This allocation is intended to support future PLX markets, exchange liquidity and broader availability.

It does not mean that 200 million PLX currently exists in exchange wallets or has already been minted.

## Community Rewards

Long-term economic planning reserves up to:

**10% — 100,000,000 PLX**

for community incentives and future ecosystem participation.

Potential uses may include:

- Community rewards
- Ecosystem incentives
- Promotional distributions
- Development participation
- Future community programs

Any future distribution program should be publicly documented before launch.

## Supply Transparency

Parallax publishes a public blockchain explorer so users, miners, exchanges and researchers can independently inspect:

- Current mined PLX supply
- Block height
- Block rewards
- Transactions
- Addresses
- Network hashrate
- Blockchain activity

Explorer:

https://explorer.parallaxcoin.xyz/

## Supply Policy Status

The **1 billion PLX figure represents the project's intended long-term economic model**.

The precise long-term emission and allocation implementation is being reviewed to ensure that published tokenomics remain aligned with the active Parallax Mainnet consensus rules.

Until that process is completed, Parallax does not describe 1 billion PLX as a currently enforced on-chain hard cap.

This distinction is intentional and is provided for transparency.

